{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540220-gmc-or-vanilla-first-time-changeling-group","id":540220,"title":"GMC or Vanilla. First time Changeling group","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-04T17:54:53-07:00","id":540220,"title":"GMC or Vanilla. First time Changeling group","content":"We decided to pick up changeling, should we try to use the gmc rules updates with it or just use the vanilla rules until 2nd edition comes out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5629-ocule","name":"Ocule","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:10:13-07:00","id":540258,"title":"","content":"If you're picking up 1e Changeling anyway, the GMC rules update is free and pretty easy to integrate into any splat game, may as well. That said, 1E changeling with the GMC updates will look pretty different from 2e changeling, so if you're just getting into Changeling now, it may be worth the wait for 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:44:11-07:00","id":540331,"title":"","content":"We were wanting to start something now. Introducing my friend to world of darkness but i have no time to run it so im kind of helping him out. He really wants to do changeling so im kind of right here walking him through how to be a ST. I already had the changeling book just never actually got a chance to play it so thought id ask ;3<br /> <br /> We were planning to upgrade to 2nd edition when it came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5629-ocule","name":"Ocule","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:54:45-07:00","id":540341,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want to start now, 1e is the way to go. All the CtL 1e books are out there to use.<br /> <br /> The issue is that it does not seem like you will be able to just move your characters from 1e to 2e rules. It shouldn't be impossible, but it will probably require a good deal of work to upgrade when it comes around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:08:37-07:00","id":540355,"title":"","content":"Yeah we were debating on trying to convert it to the gmc rules update.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5629-ocule","name":"Ocule","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T22:46:30-07:00","id":540604,"title":"","content":"And as I said in my first post, the update is free and it's pretty easy to incorporate it into a 1e changeling game. Just be aware that when 2e comes out, it's still going to be quite different than 1e changeling with the rules updates hacked in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-05-2015, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:34:56-07:00","id":540716,"title":"","content":"I use the GMC rules in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\">Malibu Dream House</a>, short of the Beat system for experience as my group prefers the 1e XP system. GMC with Changeling is pretty seamless and easy to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:57:46-07:00","id":540722,"title":"","content":"To my experience the World of Darkness is big on character concept, not classes and mechanics, and you should be able to re create your concept with the 2ed rules. Though a tweak or two might be necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:54:44-07:00","id":541206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/540220-gmc-or-vanilla-first-time-changeling-group?p=540722#post540722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my experience the World of Darkness is big on character concept, not classes and mechanics, and you should be able to re create your concept with the 2ed rules. Though a tweak or two might be necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on personal tastes, character concept is actually what might make going from 1e to 2e a little tricky for some people. 1e Seeming facilitates a certain narrative (what was done to the character), while 2e is working a different one (how the character took herself back). My guess is that this won't be a problem for converting many concepts (so long as they're willing to apply whatever 2e Seeming fits best or go with no Seeming). But if a player puts a lot of value on a character's Seeming group identity, that could be an issue. It'll depend on the group whether this is just a tweak or a big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T10:29:32-07:00","id":541429,"title":"","content":"Some of it is also an issue of continuity.<br /> <br /> If I was asked to recreate my old 1e PCs into 2e PCs in a new game with a new continuity, it would be pretty simple. Some might stay pretty much as is; though I might ask for a custom Kith since Dual Kith seems to be out of the picture. Others would end up with very different splats, and then very different powers sets from it.<br /> <br /> If you're trying to keep the same character in the same continuity, it gets much harder because there's shaping up to be a pretty big shift in things. Some characters might get close enough to their previous abilities that it's easy to gloss over the minor differences. Others aren't.<br /> <br /> This is actually something coming up in a Mage the Ascension game I'm playing in where the ST is considering changing to M20 now that we have the backer PDF for it. A few characters (mine included) have access to a Background that got a huge alteration in M20, and the book largely didn't replace the functionality of what it removed with anything else. It isn't that there aren't other paths to those specific mechanics that M20 keeps, but there's a big difference in how you play a character that has super-senses all the time and can't shut them off even if they wanted to, and a character that has access to a power that can grant them super senses when they want it.<br /> <br /> Even though from an objective stance the M20 rules on that are better, the amount of tweaking needed to convert fully to M20 compared to just bringing some of the M20 stuff into our Revised rules game is getting a hefty vote towards the later.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this is inherently going to be the case with CtL. But it's a risk depending on what mechanical widgets your players opt in on for their CtL 1e/GMC hybrid, and what changes with CtL 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:07:30-07:00","id":541551,"title":"","content":"Don't be afraid to tweak the rules instead, especially for an ongoing chronicle. If it's just at your table and the players all agree then modify the rules to keep your story going. If it proves unwieldy then don't keep it for the next chronicle. Don't let the rules get in the way of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:52:30-07:00","id":541654,"title":"","content":"If you're planning on converting, I'd use the GMC update, if for no other reason than keeping xp consistent when you change over.<br /> <br /> The second edition looks like it's going to be pretty cool, but it looks like there are going to be some pretty major changes. Not just Seemings, either. If your group would consider it, I'd suggest running a short self-contained story with the current 1e rules instead of starting a lengthy chronicle. Then, when the new edition releases, you can decide if you want to continue with those characters in 1e, make the necessary changes to upgrade those characters to 2e, or start fresh with a whole new set of characters for 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T17:31:54-07:00","id":543250,"title":"","content":"It took a little tweaking, but I spent about a year playing Changeling with the NWOD2.0 rules quite easily after playing with the 1.0 rules for a good year as well. You can't really go wrong either way, but just be aware of a few weird cases in the 2.0 rules (especially in regards to defence due to Athletics or whatever).<br /> <br /> 1.0 works solidly and is probably recommended if you're not super experienced with WoD in general, but 2.0 works fine (if a little homebrewy) for Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T08:52:30-07:00","id":543923,"title":"","content":"As others have said, there's very little difficulty in using the GMC rules update, my only caution would be that it can make certain combat powers disproportionately more effective. Armor granting contracts suddenly allow characters to soak crazy amounts of damage, and there's a skitter skulk build that can trash most True Fae at character creation. Do not allow skitter skulks with Armed Defense in court of the West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}